"""pktrec-phy - bring-up tool for the Ethernet FMC Max (OP080) port subsystem of the
FPGA Packet Recorder: DP83867 PHY configuration over the fabric MDIO master, link
status, path selection and counters (M0), PHY SFD timestamping and the per-port
hardware traffic generator / checker (M2), TAP mode: per-pair mode, dynamic
inter-frame gap, link-state propagation and forwarding latency (M3).

Hardware (include/pktrec_regs.h):
  eth_ports/pktrec_eth_ports_0  0x4_2008_0000 (512 KB)  MAC/PCS regs, MDIO master, GT APB
  eth_ports/pktrec_m0_path_0    0x4_2002_0000 (4 KB)    PATH_CTRL, counters, PHY GPIO/PG,
                                                        traffic generator + checker (GEN_*/CHK_*)
  capture/pktrec_capture_0      0x4_2003_0000 (4 KB)    SFD timestamping (PKTREC_SFD_*, 0x400..)
All are bound to generic-uio in the device tree; the tool finds them by their
physical address in /sys/class/uio/uio*/maps/map0/addr (or uses /dev/mem with
--devmem). Dependency-free: mmap + memoryview (aligned 32-bit accesses) only.

Commands:
  init [--1000-only] [--reset] [--no-sfd] [--wait S]
                         configure all four PHYs (see init_phy) and re-trigger the
                         SGMII status word on every copper link that comes up
  status [--json]        per port: PHY link/speed/duplex, SGMII/PCS state, GPIO levels
  path <port|all> idle|loop|fwd|gen   select the TX source of a port (also keeps
                         PAIR_MODE consistent: a pair is "tap" when both ports are fwd)
  mode <pair 0|1> tap|monitor [--force]   per-pair mode: tap = both ports forward to
                         each other (inline TAP), monitor = both ports receive only.
                         Refused while a capture runs (capture CTRL.ENABLE) unless --force
  mode status [--json]   PAIR_MODE, PATH_CTRL and the effective path per pair
  ifg <port|all> [--enable on|off] [--nom B] [--min B] [--hi B] [--lo B] [--json]
                         dynamic inter-frame gap of the TAP forward path: settings,
                         FWD FIFO fill (now / max), reduced-gap time and entries, FLUSH
  latency (--pair P | --in A --out B) [--count N] [--timeout S] [--window NS] [--json]
                         TAP forwarding latency per frame, TX SFD(out) - RX SFD(in), from
                         the SFD log FIFOs while paced traffic flows (one frame in flight,
                         e.g. ping -s <size> -i 0.01 through the TAP): min/median/max
  counters [--clear] [--json]   M0 frame counters
  sfd status [--json] [--clear]   SFD timestamping: edges, matches, stale, mismatches,
                         MAC->SFD deltas, TX latency, latest timestamps per port
  sfd config [--rx-win MIN MAX] [--tx-win MIN MAX] [--rx-offset P NS] [--tx-offset P NS]
             [--match on|off] [--log on|off] [--min-low CYC] [--min-high CYC]
  sfd log <port> [--dir rx|tx] [--json]   pop the port's SFD log FIFO (needs --log on)
  gen <port> start [--size B] [--count N] [--ifg B | --rate PPS] [--raw] [--etype E]
             [--dst MAC] [--src MAC] [--stream ID] [--seq-first N] [--rand-mask M]
             [--no-select]   start the port's generator (selects PATH gen unless --no-select)
  gen <port> stop | status [--json]
  chk <port> start [--raw] [--etype E] | stop | status [--json]   receive checker
  (--size is the wire size INCLUDING the FCS, like test/gen_seq.py: 64..16387)
  watch [--interval S] [--no-propagate] [--debounce S] [--grace S] [--json]
                         re-trigger the SGMII status word (CFG2[7] 0->1) whenever a
                         PHY's copper link changes (DP83867 sends it only once), and
                         for pairs in TAP mode propagate link state: when a port's
                         copper link stays down for --debounce s, power down its
                         partner PHY (BMCR[11]) so the device on the other side sees
                         link down too; power it up again (and re-trigger SGMII) when
                         the port comes back. Ports we powered down never propagate,
                         and a port just powered up gets --grace s to negotiate before
                         its link-down counts (no ping-pong). Every action is logged
                         (--json: one JSON object per line). On exit, or when the
                         pair leaves TAP mode, every PHY it powered down is powered up.
  mdio <phy> <reg> [val] raw PHY register access (phy: p0..p3 or MDIO address;
                         reg > 0x1f uses the extended REGCR/ADDAR indirection)

There is one MDIO master for the four PHYs: every MDIO access (including the
4-step extended-register sequences and read-modify-writes) holds an flock on
/run/lock/pktrec-mdio, so 'watch' (pktrec-phy-watch.service) and CLI commands
never interleave on the bus.
"""

